# STURR.OBJ - the ZSU-23-4 "Shilka" TURRET: the boxy drum, the four 23 mm
# barrels stacked two over two on the right cheek, and the Gun Dish radar
# hinged up off the roof behind them. Drawn at the SAME world point as
# SHULL.OBJ but on its OWN yaw, exactly the way the radar station's dish
# turns on the mast - so this model's origin is the TURRET RING, on the
# vehicle's centreline at ground level.
#
# Same frame and same scale as SHULL.OBJ: -Z forward, Y up, one unit =
# 0.2 m, converted at -s 3. The deck it sits on is at y=7 there, so the
# turret floor is at y=7 here; roof 12 (2.4 m), dish top 18 (3.6 m).
#
# MODELDRAW YAWS ONLY - it cannot pitch - so the barrels are BAKED at
# zero elevation and level: the turret's yaw is the whole of the tracking.
# The brief costed the alternatives; this is the honest cheap one.
#
# 8 vertices / 5 faces - just the drum now. It was 25/15 and full; the Gun
# Dish left for SDISH.OBJ and the barrels for SBARR.OBJ, because all three
# move differently: the radar sweeps, the drum tracks, the guns tilt. A
# model carries ONE transform, so three motions need three models.
o sturr

# ---- the drum: a box with the front plate raked back a little -------------
v -5.5000 7.0000 7.0000
v 5.5000 7.0000 7.0000
v 5.5000 12.0000 7.0000
v -5.5000 12.0000 7.0000
v -5.5000 7.0000 -6.0000
v 5.5000 7.0000 -6.0000
v 5.5000 11.2000 -6.0000
v -5.5000 11.2000 -6.0000

# ---- the drum ------------------------------------------------------------
usemtl PAL17
f 4 3 7 8
usemtl PAL0
f 5 6 7 8
usemtl PAL16
f 1 4 8 5
f 2 3 7 6
f 1 2 3 4
